  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml states no <repository>.",
        "  <repository> is the only machine-readable link from a published release back to the source it was built from. Without it nothing that reads the release can tell where its source is.",
        "  <website> is not set either."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "link-dead",
      "lines": [
        "8 links of appinfo/info.xml lead nowhere:",
        "  <screenshot> https://abload.de/img/bildschirmfotoam2021-u7j37.png: HTTP 410, after a redirect to https://abload.de/ende.html",
        "  <screenshot> https://abload.de/img/bildschirmfotoam2021-m0jq9.png: HTTP 410, after a redirect to https://abload.de/ende.html",
        "  <screenshot> https://abload.de/img/bildschirmfotoam2021-6dj9p.png: HTTP 410, after a redirect to https://abload.de/ende.html",
        "  <screenshot> https://abload.de/img/bildschirmfotoam2021-otj7x.png: HTTP 410, after a redirect to https://abload.de/ende.html",
        "  <screenshot> https://abload.de/img/bildschirmfotoam2021-kykd8.png: HTTP 410, after a redirect to https://abload.de/ende.html",
        "  <screenshot> https://abload.de/img/bildschirmfotoam2021-nbk8s.png: HTTP 410, after a redirect to https://abload.de/ende.html",
        "  <screenshot> https://abload.de/img/bildschirmfotoam2021-vuk8t.png: HTTP 410, after a redirect to https://abload.de/ende.html",
        "  <screenshot> https://abload.de/img/bildschirmfotoam2021-03kxw.png: HTTP 410, after a redirect to https://abload.de/ende.html",
        "  The App Store page shows these links as they are; a reader who follows one ends on an error page."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "The licence is stated differently: agpl (appinfo/info.xml), ISC (js/package.json), AGPL (composer.json).",
        "  Whoever redistributes the app has to pick one of them, and the App Store shows the one from info.xml.",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. With min-version 31 info.xml can state an SPDX id instead.",
        "  No SPDX id: AGPL (composer.json). Only an SPDX id says which licence is meant, and for a GNU licence whether -only or -or-later.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 31 to 35; the oldest maintained major is 33 (the Maintenance and Release Schedule of nextcloud/server), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  min-version 31 reaches below the oldest maintained major (33), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "No Node version is stated: no engines.node, no .nvmrc, and no node-version in the installed workflows.",
        "  Whoever builds the app uses whatever Node they have, and a build that works on one machine is then not evidence for the next."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: PHPUnit (phpunit.xml).",
        " No ESLint configuration: nothing checks the frontend sources, so a wrong import is found by the build or not at all.",
        " No Stylelint configuration: stylesheets are unchecked, and a mistake in CSS fails silently instead of loudly.",
        " No Psalm configuration: the PHP side has no static analysis, which is what catches a wrong type before the server does.",
        " No PHP-CS-Fixer configuration: no coding standard is applied to the PHP sources, so formatting is settled in review instead of by a command.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "1 declared package is named nowhere in the checkout: @nextcloud/browserslist-config.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 77 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "lockfiles",
      "lines": [
        "js/package-lock.json (lockfileVersion 3) and composer.lock in the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "ncmake-bootstrap",
      "lines": [
        "The ncmake bootstrap stub is in place (21 lines).",
        "  make reads GNUmakefile and never Makefile; it runs only with make -f <name>."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "Every directory the shipped PHP reaches through __DIR__ and the frontend through linkTo is in the shipped file set."
      ]
    }
  ],
